{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(2,-5,1)$, $P(4,-2,3)$ and $Q(5,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-33142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨2,-5,1⟩,\\,p=⟨4,-2,3⟩,$ and $q=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,3⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,2⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨5,1,0⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-15i+8j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-15,8,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z+67 & =0 \\\\ 15x-8y-3z-67 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-33142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4dfa0264a7b6da1ba9e8b933a43c195d9359a9a9beda6e5f88438a79bcbb6ae"} {"question" "q-33142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-33142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15x-8y-3z+70=0"] ["math" "15x-8y-3z-67=0"] ["math" "2x-5y+z-70=0"] ["math" "4x-2y+3z=0"] ["math" "5x+y-67=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-33142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15x-8y-3z-67=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $2x-y+2z+6=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$ \n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,$\n{{field-2}}\n, \n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨2,-1,2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z+6 & =0 \\\\ z & =-x+\\frac{y}{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-3)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-3⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-3⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-1,2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4dfa0264a7b6da1ba9e8b933a43c195d9359a9a9beda6e5f88438a79bcbb6ae"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-326901" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=1-4t \\\\ z=-3-2t\\end{aligned}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-4y\\,-\\,$ \n{{field-2}} $z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$\\,=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,5⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =⟨1,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4dfa0264a7b6da1ba9e8b933a43c195d9359a9a9beda6e5f88438a79bcbb6ae"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336110" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$3x\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$y\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,1⟩.$  From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-5,2⟩.$  So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-5,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =⟨-2,3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4dfa0264a7b6da1ba9e8b933a43c195d9359a9a9beda6e5f88438a79bcbb6ae"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336201" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "19"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the Cartesian equation $5x+2y+z-4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨$\n{{field-2}} $,\\,2\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨5,2,1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y+z-4 & =0 \\\\ z & =-5x-2y+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,\\,2\\,,1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4dfa0264a7b6da1ba9e8b933a43c195d9359a9a9beda6e5f88438a79bcbb6ae"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"} {"question" "q-336228" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14078229/state.json" "file_sha256" "28409862a4604b8767f90616905146a3519524afe8640227b900af580efae445"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2810 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
